    {
      "id": "p0238-b005",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "source": {
        "text": "As we've already seen in the Japanese script, Flowey has used the boyish pronoun boku throughout the game so far. For first-time players, boku seems to reflect Flowey's friendly personality at the beginning of the game. However, there's another reason that Flowey uses boku: it turns out that he's actually the king's young son, stuck in the body of a flower.",
        "raw": "As we've already seen in the Japanese script, Flowey has used the boyish\npronoun boku throughout the game so far. For first-time players, boku seems\nto reflect Flowey's friendly personality at the beginning of the game. However,\nthere's another reason that Flowey uses boku: it turns out that he's actually the\nking's young son, stuck in the body of a flower.",
        "status": "corrected",
        "languages": [
          "en"
        ],
        "bbox": [
          0.29511051,
          0.21541429,
          0.89545593,
          0.30027143
        ],
        "mask_bbox": [
